WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:01.728
From above, a field is a shape.

00:01.948 --> 00:05.873
On the ground, it becomes decisions
about soil, plants and water.

00:06.093 --> 00:09.027
GX FieldOS keeps those
observations together, so

00:09.027 --> 00:11.960
each can inform the next field task.

00:12.000 --> 00:15.125
For this Abidjan example,
the owner declares two

00:15.125 --> 00:18.251
point five hectares and saves a GPS point.

00:18.471 --> 00:21.628
Neither an image nor one
coordinate proves the area.

00:21.920 --> 00:23.925
A later walk can refine the boundary.

00:26.000 --> 00:28.432
We create five folders
with four views each.

00:28.652 --> 00:31.991
Twenty example images stay
grouped by site, soil,

00:31.991 --> 00:35.329
plants, water and field
edge, with their context.

00:35.549 --> 00:38.280
The team can revisit the
original views later.

00:38.550 --> 00:41.654
Each folder follows one
subject through four views,

00:41.654 --> 00:44.758
giving the model context
beyond a single close-up.

00:47.350 --> 00:50.411
That lets the team compare
site, soil, plants,

00:50.411 --> 00:53.473
water and field edge without
mixing their evidence.

00:53.720 --> 00:55.256
The five sets stay distinct.

00:57.000 --> 01:00.072
The Meta Model API examines all five sets.

01:00.292 --> 01:04.335
GX reports five analyzed scans
and keeps observations beside

01:04.335 --> 01:08.377
source images, so the team
can trace each suggestion.

01:08.550 --> 01:10.587
The boundary result points back to its

01:10.587 --> 01:12.625
source views, ready for a field check.

01:12.870 --> 01:15.025
This points the team to
the next field checks.

01:17.000 --> 01:18.664
A clue can guide a site visit.

01:18.884 --> 01:21.295
It cannot measure soil chemistry, confirm

01:21.295 --> 01:23.705
a disease cause or guarantee harvest.

01:23.925 --> 01:25.888
Field checks come before investment.

01:26.100 --> 01:28.489
The owner decides what to verify first.

01:29.000 --> 01:32.709
The results feed a
versioned plan draft: site

01:32.709 --> 01:35.955
assessment, preparation, planting,
maintenance, harvest and sale.

01:36.175 --> 01:38.436
The owner reviews it before field work.

01:38.650 --> 01:42.981
New field evidence can prompt a revision
while preserving the earlier plan.

01:45.000 --> 01:49.096
The budget links nine planned
operations to dates, costs and sales.

01:49.316 --> 01:53.060
Conservative, base and favorable
scenarios test illustrative

01:53.060 --> 01:56.804
inputs, never guaranteed
market prices or returns.

01:57.024 --> 02:00.672
Actual entries can replace
estimates as work progresses.

02:03.000 --> 02:07.907
GX downloads the business plan as
Word and PDF, then the Excel tracker.

02:08.127 --> 02:11.881
Their excerpts show planned
operations, cash flow and

02:11.881 --> 02:15.167
scenarios, with illustrative
assumptions visible for review.

02:15.400 --> 02:18.244
The tracker separates plans
from actuals, ready for

02:18.244 --> 02:20.733
costs and sales recorded in the field.

02:20.900 --> 02:23.609
Actuals can be recorded
as the work proceeds.

02:24.000 --> 02:28.288
GX then downloads the technical
guide as PDF and Word.

02:28.508 --> 02:32.229
Its labeled excerpts show
equipment, materials, procedures and

02:32.229 --> 02:35.484
field controls drawn
from the exported files.

02:35.650 --> 02:38.743
The guide gives the team a
checklist for the next site visit.

02:41.000 --> 02:43.709
GX links field evidence
to action and budget.
